<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal: thousands still missing as flood recovery begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4168f3bafaadad1c02c7ef156b05bef17c2bbd9d66b989997dc290b7356b0bd0</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-flood-recovery-begins/a-79259980--8e8d61a072b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-flood-recovery-begins/a-79259980?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Himalayan nation is moving from rescue operations to recovery, facing a $4.8 billion reconstruction bill amid renewed calls for climate justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urge unity after Russian strike on train</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c14109b0b6ccea24ecf020c93558895b3f1ffb8c36179d8b61e1cf76818dbea</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807--826cde282d81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's drone attack on a train near the Ukraine-Poland border has triggered EU calls to up support for Kyiv. Allies of Ukraine should show they "are not scared," said the bloc's top diplomat, Kaja Kallas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pay to ghost your boss: Japan's resignation business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85ed0968d6f60e45ecb46449c7102b8763e2aaf40546be39cf4233a9435c0711</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584--1937a091cd92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Resignation agencies in Japan help employees leave their jobs seamlessly in just 15 minutes. Young people are especially eager to use their services.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli minister accuses 'NAZA' filmmakers of 'treason'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe6e87065da58a33ffa42e43bbcf0c996248b29f959154f0f2e7de2e36f3ba2d</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860--3831f9d14cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel's culture minister wants to strip the makers of a documentary on Israel's Gaza offensive of their citizenship. He accused the two of seeking "applause from antisemites around the world."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17dcce4d985c5a284280ee283ae1de2fbf71f5998851ac0bfe26c0045362aa81</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:beaf92a33b0e4bb231582cab3a4563228b539083d01c835e279e330ac55ef4cd</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a233f7beb55e8d9211dc9e48bc0b5391482fc93426005213b49f7c06b016d957</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump visits Ireland, says unification would be 'fantastic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:458096e6f77cc133777af1c02254b06b891f75e531d48ee966dffda0de2ddc31</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685--23dd10281a51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's trip to Ireland to watch a golf tournament has also included meetings with leaders there.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda lays 'boy king' Oyo to rest amid succession row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8414a4e4ab2492a4a003e4bf59c91575f8c9f8a3f0547b91fd49a3de029b2c01</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428--755cb45ab2c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uganda has buried King Oyo Nyimba, who was crowned in the Tooro Kingdom in 1995 aged just 3. His death at 34 has triggered a dispute over a successor, as rumors abound of possible heirs born out of wedlock.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uber leaves 2 key African markets — and drivers in despair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d75febe91341d0aef8ef2052d669a057e044f7b1b08a0330f8e9061f9f6c253e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-2-key-african-markets-and-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189--6991d13e0e30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-2-key-african-markets-and-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uber's departure from Nigeria and Uganda has left countless customers high and dry. But what about drivers? With fuel prices, maintenance, and other operating costs rising, many say they're struggling to make a living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's drone war comes to Moldova and Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bf53e38d45f37393eb826a007d8ac42204a95593b33e73a7105cfba7c7940bd</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591--15076a5f335b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Incursions by Russian drones into Moldovan and Romanian airspace are increasingly common. This week the Ukrainian president's plane was stopped from taking off from Chisinau. Observers suspect the attacks are deliberate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW exclusive: Zelenskyy offers to meet Putin at G20 in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:476d351186d6a04a054d05c2ca7dbe8425ed47ad8622aa937d4dfdd75a12efc6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703--3aacfd955f7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an interview with DW, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said his country was in a strong position to negotiate and offered to meet Vladimir Putin in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran pursues cautious escalation ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56552e0fac3024dad2715130c103ae01af136ae53cf019b09629d92be481a6fa</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061--fcf56cfd7af3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tehran appears to be boosting pressure on Washington ahead of the crucial midterm vote, but shows little desire to return to a full-scale war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
